lisher","DOI":"10.1109\/FG.2018.00019"},{"key":"ref19","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.21437\/Interspeech.2024-788"},{"key":"ref20","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/ACII.2019.8925444"},{"key":"ref21","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1109\/ICIP40778.2020.9191019"}],"event":{"name":"ICASSP 2026 - 2026 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)","location":"Barcelona, Spain","start":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,3]]},"end":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,8]]}},"container-title":["ICASSP 2026 - 2026 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)"],"link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/xplorestaging.ieee.org\/ielx8\/11460365\/11460314\/11462815.pdf?arnumber=11462815","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,22]],"date-time":"2026-04-22T07:32:48Z","timestamp":1776843168000},"score":64.11748,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/ieeexplore.ieee.org\/document\/11462815\/"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,3]]},"references-count":21,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/icassp55912.2026.11462815","published":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,3]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,5,1]],"date-time":"2026-05-01T22:24:43Z","timestamp":1777674283557,"version":"3.51.4"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"The Institute of Electronics Engineers of Korea","issue":"4","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ieie"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,30]]},"DOI":"10.5573\/ieie.2026.63.4.110","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,29]],"date-time":"2026-04-29T08:11:17Z","timestamp":1777450277000},"page":"110-116","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Cross-Attention Fusion for Audio-Visual Multimodal Emotion Recognition"],"prefix":"10.5573","volume":"63","author":[{"given":"Jeong-Yoon","family":"Kim","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Seung-Ho","family":"Lee","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"3531","container-title":["Journal of the Institute of Electronics and Information Engineers"],"original-title":["\uc624\ub514\uc624-\ube44\uc8fc\uc5bc \uba40\ud2f0\ubaa8\ub2ec \uac10\uc815 \uc778\uc2dd\uc744 \uc704\ud55c Cross-Attention Fusion"],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,29]],"date-time":"2026-04-29T08:11:29Z","timestamp":1777450289000},"score":45.4537,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/www.dbpia.co.kr\/Journal\/ArticleDetail\/NODE12744255"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,30]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"4","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,30]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.5573\/ieie.2026.63.4.110","ISSN":["2287-5026","2288-159X"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2287-5026","type":"print"},{"value":"2288-159X","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,30]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,5]],"date-time":"2026-10-05T21:17:00Z","timestamp":1791235020996,"version":"4.1.0"},"reference-count":89,"publisher":"MDPI AG","issue":"7","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,27]],"date-time":"2025-03-27T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1743033600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"name":"Technology Innovation Program","award":["RS-2024-00487049"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["RS-2024-00487049"]}]},{"name":"Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy (MOTIE, Korea)","award":["RS-2024-00487049"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["RS-2024-00487049"]}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Mathematics"],"abstract":"<jats:p>Multimodal emotion recognition involves leveraging complementary relationships across modalities to enhance the assessment of human emotions. Networks that integrate diverse information sources outperform single-modal approaches while offering greater robustness against noisy or missing data. Current emotion recognition approaches often rely on cross-modal attention mechanisms, particularly audio and visual modalities; however, these methods do not assume the complementary nature of the data. Despite making this assumption, it is not uncommon to see non-complementary relationships arise in real-world data, reducing the effectiveness of feature integration that assumes consistent complementarity. While audio\u2013visual co-learning provides a broader understanding of contextual information for practical implementation, discrepancies between audio and visual data, such as semantic inconsistencies, pose challenges and lay the groundwork for inaccurate predictions. In this way, they have limitations in modeling the intramodal and cross-modal interactions. In order to address these problems, we propose a multimodal learning framework for emotion recognition, called the Hybrid Multi-ATtention Network (HMATN). Specifically, we introduce a collaborative cross-attentional paradigm for audio\u2013visual amalgamation, intending to effectively capture salient features over modalities while preserving both intermodal and intramodal relationships. The model calculates cross-attention weights by analyzing the relationship between combined feature illustrations and distinct modes. Meanwhile, the network employs the Hybrid Attention of Single and Parallel Cross-Modal (HASPCM) mechanism, comprising a single-modal attention component and a parallel cross-modal attention component, to harness complementary multimodal data and hidden features to improve representation. Additionally, these modules exploit complementary and concealed multimodal information to enhance the richness of feature representation. Finally, the efficiency of the proposed method is demonstrated through experiments on complex videos from the AffWild2 and AFEW-VA datasets. The findings of these tests show that the developed attentional audio\u2013visual fusion model offers a cost-efficient solution that surpasses state-of-the-art techniques, even when the input data are noisy or missing modalities.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3390\/math13071100","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,27]],"date-time":"2025-03-27T12:41:02Z","timestamp":1743079262000},"page":"1100","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/mdpi_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":34,"title":["Hybrid Multi-Attention Network for Audio\u2013Visual Emotion Recognition Through Multimodal Feature Fusion"],"prefix":"10.3390","volume":"13","author":[{"given":"Sathishkumar","family":"Moorthy","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Artificial Intelligence Data Science, Sejong University, Seoul 05006, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Yeon-Kug","family":"Moon","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Artificial Intelligence Data Science, Sejong University, Seoul 05006, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1968","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,3,27]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"109606","DOI":"10.1016\/j.engappai.2024.109606","article-title":"Hybrid multi-attention transformer for robust video object detection","volume":"139","author":"Moorthy","year":"2025","journal-title":"Eng. Appl. Artif. Intell."},{"key":"ref_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"360","DOI":"10.1016\/j.neunet.2023.08.019","article-title":"Learning dynamic spatial-temporal regularized correlation filter tracking with response deviation suppression via multi-feature fusion","volume":"167","author":"Moorthy","year":"2023","journal-title":"Neural Netw."},{"key":"ref_3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"155","DOI":"10.1186\/s13677-024-00718-5","article-title":"Building integrated assessment model for IoT techno